{
  "comment": "Claude Code 2.1.330 built-in tool outputs whose fields the host checks, for #612. The Read union (text, image, notebook, pdf, parts), Write's `type`, Grep's `mode` and NotebookEdit's `cell_type` follow that version's output schema, as do the enums added for #599: REPL's `stoppedBy` and `neverRan`, Poll's `provenance[].authority`, the `gitDiff.status` of Write and Edit, Skill's `status` and Bash's `gitOperation` kinds and actions. `Eval` is the REPL name the bundle also accepts (`li()`); no recorded transcript has an Eval event yet; the Read `parts` case with `pages` is the shape a live PostToolUse hook received for a PDF read with a page range. Paths, sizes and image bytes are stand-ins. {{SECRET}} becomes the planted marker when the test runs, and only content-bearing fields carry it. `words` lists the paths of the fields the host reads as one of a few values; a replacement must keep them as they were, keep the type of every value, keep every number and keep a file path that equals the one in tool_input. `schemas` is the 2.1.330 output schema of each tool with a fixed last-resort replacement in claude-tool-outputs.json: a dotted path to its kind (`any` takes every kind) and, under `words`, the values the schema allows for an enum field.",
